From 55f47027b4a18f04fae9f19ac969c5bb4cfc282d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:27:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: RISCV64: name OR and AND by namespace in the
 disassembler

Need the bug URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

disassembleOpcode() pulls in namespace RISCV64Instructions with a
using-directive and lists the instruction types by their bare names.
JavaScriptCorePrefix.h includes CodeBlock.h, which reaches
ParserTokens.h, so a build using the precompiled prefix header also
sees the JSTokenType enumerators JSC::OR and JSC::AND in this file.
The bare names OR and AND are then ambiguous, and GCC rejects the
template argument list with "template argument 36 is invalid".

Name the two instruction types with their namespace, as
RTypeDefaultFormatting in this file does.

* Source/JavaScriptCore/disassembler/RISCV64Disassembler.cpp:
(JSC::RISCV64Disassembler::disassembleOpcode):

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 Source/JavaScriptCore/disassembler/RISCV64Disassembler.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/disassembler/RISCV64Disassembler.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/disassembler/RISCV64Disassembler.cpp
@@ -584,7 +584,7 @@ CString disassembleOpcode(uint32_t *pc)
         LB, LH, LW, LBU, LHU,
         SB, SH, SW,
         ADDI, SLTI, SLTIU, XORI, ORI, ANDI, SLLI, SRLI, SRAI,
-        ADD, SUB, SLL, SLT, SLTU, XOR, SRL, SRA, OR, AND,
+        ADD, SUB, SLL, SLT, SLTU, XOR, SRL, SRA, RISCV64Instructions::OR, RISCV64Instructions::AND,
         FENCE, ECALL, EBREAK,
         // RV64I Base Instruction Set (in addition to RV32I)
         LWU, LD, SD,
